      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's just an emotional bias. you're adding variables like \"curiosity\" or \"connection\" to make the equation look better, but those are just temporary spikes in a long-term trend that always goes to zero. if we look at the logic strictly, if the outcome is guaranteed to be null, then there's no mathematical difference between staying or leaving. both paths lead to the same result. so why is one considered \"better\" than the other if the net value is identical? it feels like we're just lying to ourselves to stay in the loop.",
